# ASUS ROG Xbox Ally (RC73YA) and Xbox Ally X (RC73XA): the built-in gamepad on
# a kernel without ASUS's Ally HID driver, where the generic HID driver reads it.
#
# The pad declares 14 buttons in XInput order (A B X Y LB RB View Menu L3 R3
# Xbox, then three of unknown meaning), and hid-input gives HID button N the
# code BTN_GAMEPAD+N-1, so from X on each button arrives under the code of
# another one (View as BTN_TL, R3 as BTN_TR2, the Xbox button as BTN_SELECT,
# ...). This entry has the kernel report the codes of an Xbox controller
# instead, to every program that reads the pad, and parks the three unknown
# buttons on BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY1..3 so they cannot pass for a standard button.
#
# The order is derived from two independent projects plus one observation, not
# yet confirmed by a physical press test: Handheld Daemon's Ally X button map
# and InputPlumber's former Ally X fallback map (both for USB id 0b05:1b4c),
# and the Xbox button seen as BTN_SELECT on an RC73YA.
#
# Scancode = HID usage (page 0x09, button N). The match is limited to the
# gamepad interface (input5, EV bitmap 1b) on these two boards. Omarchy Game
# Mode never installs it; as root:
#   install -Dm644 61-rog-xbox-ally-gamepad.hwdb /etc/udev/hwdb.d/61-rog-xbox-ally-gamepad.hwdb
#   systemd-hwdb update
# then reboot, so that the pad is set up with it. Applying it to the running
# pad (udevadm trigger --action=change --subsystem-match=input) is only safe
# with every button released: the codes move one button at a time, and a
# button held meanwhile can stay down under its old code (a held Xbox button
# stays down as View until View is pressed and released).
# To undo, remove that file, run systemd-hwdb update and reboot: the kernel
# keeps the codes it was given until the pad is created again. Remove it as
# well once the kernel has ASUS's Ally HID driver.
evdev:name:ASUSTeK Computer Inc. N-KEY Device:phys:*/input5:ev:1b:dmi:*:rnRC73[XY]A:*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_90003=btn_north
 KEYBOARD_KEY_90004=btn_west
 KEYBOARD_KEY_90005=btn_tl
 KEYBOARD_KEY_90006=btn_tr
 KEYBOARD_KEY_90007=btn_select
 KEYBOARD_KEY_90008=btn_start
 KEYBOARD_KEY_90009=btn_thumbl
 KEYBOARD_KEY_9000a=btn_thumbr
 KEYBOARD_KEY_9000b=btn_mode
 KEYBOARD_KEY_9000c=btn_trigger_happy1
 KEYBOARD_KEY_9000d=btn_trigger_happy2
 KEYBOARD_KEY_9000e=btn_trigger_happy3
